WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.899 --> 00:00:07.140
Hi, I'm Ed Mazria.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:12.679
I'm with a non-profit organization and think-tank
called Architecture 2030.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:17.240
I'm actually right down the hill here in Santa
Fe.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:26.460
I'm here at the Global Sustainability Summer
program and I'm teaching one of the sessions,

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:31.499
and one of the things we're focusing on in
the sessions is how to really get a handle

00:00:31.499 --> 00:00:36.000
on the built environment, and especially the
building sector, when it comes to climate

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.000
change.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.000
So, how are we going to reduce emissions?

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.860
How are we going to get to a 50% reduction
by 2030 and then phase out all CO2 emissions

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:48.800
in the built environment by 2050?

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:55.710
So we've gone through all that today, in a
seminar format, and the participants that

00:00:55.710 --> 00:01:00.140
come here then work on problems on how to
do that.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:07.530
So we've issued some problems, we've illustrated
how we've done it, but we want to see what

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:14.780
other ideas come out of this and what the
students and the participants bring to the

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:16.080
problems that we need to solve.

